#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build and display the isolated Aureon KDE desktop preview.

This developer tool is deliberately separate from ``aureon-dev test-smoke``.
It creates a new bootable *virtual* disk and a new copy-on-write QEMU overlay,
then opens that overlay in a GTK window through WSLg.  It never accepts a host
disk, shares a host directory with the guest, creates a guest NIC, installs
anything into Windows, or changes the Windows boot configuration.

The first build downloads the explicitly listed Fedora desktop packages into
the dedicated WSL Podman store.  That is why execution requires both
``--execute`` and ``--allow-build-network``.  Conversion and the guest itself
run with networking disabled.
"""

